        "fr-extract.jsonl": [
            {
                "entry_id": "229acce2-5a23-34d2-bf0e-ff9b694da03f",
                "word": "victorieusement",
                "pos": "adv",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "3fd0d62e-88b1-3cdb-bfcc-256a1970a5de",
                        "entry_id": "229acce2-5a23-34d2-bf0e-ff9b694da03f",
                        "glosses": [
                            "D’une manière victorieuse, avec un très grand avantage."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "bdd25cb5-8e41-4be2-befd-9d88dfbdc340",
                                "sense_id": "3fd0d62e-88b1-3cdb-bfcc-256a1970a5de",
                                "text": "Néanmoins, quand les deux rivales s’en allaient, on trouvait le dialogue spirituel, ce qui prouve assez victorieusement l’excellence de la pièce."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "b7d147da-0b81-4684-bd39-d8da04a982fc",
                                "sense_id": "3fd0d62e-88b1-3cdb-bfcc-256a1970a5de",
                                "text": "Mais ces deux gros industriels […] ont un titre de gloire peu commun : voici quelques années, ils ont résisté victorieusement aux assauts répétés de Robert Hersant qui, comme il l'a fait un peu partout en France, a tenté de les mettre à genoux pour racheter leurs journaux."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "6bc8e365-66a5-4285-b12d-73fa0872140c",
                                "sense_id": "3fd0d62e-88b1-3cdb-bfcc-256a1970a5de",
                                "text": "Thomasson, d’un amour de volée décroisée, s’est rattrapé de son erreur sur le but londonien, avant qu’Élie Wahi ne reprenne victorieusement un centre de Frankowski."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "43e19efd-a023-4031-b25b-6ec9181f3653",
                        "source_entry_id": "229acce2-5a23-34d2-bf0e-ff9b694da03f",
                        "source_sense_id": "3fd0d62e-88b1-3cdb-bfcc-256a1970a5de",
                        "target_lang_word": "triumphantly",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "triumphantly",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "56a7cdee-ed18-3c5c-b4fa-a3c2d1c6b29b",
                                        "entry_id": "649ae110-4b64-3cc2-9eeb-e589379d526c",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "In a triumphant manner."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "e41cc986-b9e1-4ee6-a0ff-0cd08cf13f01",
                                                "sense_id": "56a7cdee-ed18-3c5c-b4fa-a3c2d1c6b29b",
                                                "text": "Hath not the same fierce heirdom given\nRome to the Caesar—this to me?\nThe heritage of a kingly mind,\nAnd a proud spirit which hath striven\nTriumphantly with human kind."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0f08e40e-94cf-499a-b440-c943a901e64a",
                                                "sense_id": "56a7cdee-ed18-3c5c-b4fa-a3c2d1c6b29b",
                                                "text": "“Another double,” said the old lady: triumphantly making a memorandum of the circumstance, by placing one sixpence and a battered halfpenny, under the candlestick."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ab717204-1aa9-4a12-a64a-54f2a67d7635",
                                                "sense_id": "56a7cdee-ed18-3c5c-b4fa-a3c2d1c6b29b",
                                                "text": "\"Spuds - Jim - Jimmy?\" he ran his fingers reflectively through his hair, and frowned. \"Bowles,\" he added triumphantly."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ab2fe497-7059-40d2-b079-887d371609ea",
                                                "sense_id": "56a7cdee-ed18-3c5c-b4fa-a3c2d1c6b29b",
                                                "text": "All around the Giants are signs and symbols of change and progression, from the once-isolated head coach, who was spotted Sunday night triumphantly bearhugging a player, to the acutely boyish quarterback, who stepped to the podium wearing the flattering look of whiskered grunge."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "d78030ab-cf4d-4bf0-9631-cb4d37dc93ad",
                        "source_entry_id": "229acce2-5a23-34d2-bf0e-ff9b694da03f",
